[COMMENTS]
STATION,Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume in IH/UKCEH research catchment. Natural flow regime. Discontinued in June 1999. GENERAL: Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume designed by Hydraulics Research Ltd, suitable for streams with steep gradients, heavy sediment loads and high flood/drought flow ratios. Catchment nested within Cefn Brwyn (55008). Primary 15 minute dataset available. STATION HYDROMETRY: Shoal formation common, requiring prompt removal to avoid drowning. Gauged by c/m, and volumetrically at lowest flows. FLOW RECORD: Daily mean flows replaced from 01/10/1973 to 03/02/1999, and AMAXs flow from 01/10/1973 to 03/02/1999 following detailed QC (August 2025, WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Responsive flow regime. Natural to within 10% at Q95.
CATCHMENT,Very wet catchment; drains Plynlimon massif. Composed of Ordovician grits, shales and slates and Silurian mudstones. Heath on peaty plateau; grassland on free draining slopes (supporting sheep grazing) and mires in valley bottoms.
Qmed Suitability,No rating or gaugings available.
Pooling Suitability,No rating or gaugings available.
